<h1>Git, GitHub and GitHub Pages</h1>
<p class="lede">How the source code is versioned and published, the branches and tags this project uses, how the free demo site is deployed by GitHub Actions, and safe habits that protect working code.</p>

<h2>Git in five ideas</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Repository</strong>: a folder whose full history Git remembers.</li>
  <li><strong>Commit</strong>: a saved snapshot with a message (<code>git commit -m "…"</code>). Each has an id like <code>dcb9cb2</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Branch</strong>: a movable name pointing at a line of commits (<code>main</code>, <code>feature/…</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Tag</strong>: a fixed name for one commit, used to mark releases (<code>v1-local-stable</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Remote</strong>: a copy elsewhere (GitHub, called <code>origin</code>); <code>git push</code> sends commits there, <code>git pull</code> fetches them.</li>
</ol>

<h2>This project's branches and tags</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Name</th><th>Kind</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code>main</code></td><td>branch</td><td>stable Local edition and the Pages demo; every push deploys the demo</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>v1-local-stable</code></td><td>tag</td><td>the exact working state before the Cloud edition began</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>backup/local-stable</code></td><td>branch</td><td>a second safety copy of that state</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>feature/cloudflare-web-edition</code></td><td>branch</td><td>the Cloud edition, developed separately until merged</td></tr>
</table>
<script type="application/json" class="diagram" data-kind="flow" data-caption="Branches. The feature branch started from the tagged commit and has not changed main.">
