</script>
<p>The feature branch was checked out in a separate folder with <code>git worktree</code>, so the running local app (served from the main folder) was never disturbed while the Cloud edition was built.</p>
<pre><code>git tag -a v1-local-stable -m "Stable local edition"
git branch backup/local-stable
git worktree add -b feature/cloudflare-web-edition ../jira-bug-dashboard-cloud main</code></pre>

<h2>Everyday commands</h2>
<pre><code>git status                         # what changed
git add path/to/file               # stage specific files (avoid "git add ." without looking)
git commit -m "Explain the change"
git push origin feature/…          # publish the branch
git log --oneline -5               # recent history
git diff --cached                  # review what you are about to commit</code></pre>

<h2>Safe habits</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Never commit secrets. <code>.gitignore</code> lists <code>.dev.vars</code>, <code>node_modules</code>, <code>dist</code>, <code>site</code>, <code>dist-assets</code>, <code>.wrangler</code>. Before each commit, review <code>git diff --cached</code>.</li>
  <li>Never force-push shared branches, never reset away commits you did not make.</li>
  <li>Tag before big changes; work on a branch; merge only after tests pass.</li>
  <li>Ask before pushing if someone else owns the repository (pushing is visible to everyone).</li>
</ul>

<h2>GitHub Pages: the free demo</h2>
<p><code>.github/workflows/pages.yml</code> runs on every push to <code>main</code>:</p>
<pre><code>on: { push: { branches: [main] } }
jobs:
  deploy:
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run build:site          # tsc + copy public/ and dist/client/ into site/
      - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3   (path: site)
      - uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4</code></pre>
<p>One-time setup: repository <em>Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions</em>. Without that, the deploy step fails with "Ensure GitHub Pages has been enabled" (exactly what happened the first time). Result: <code>https://shouryasengar.github.io/jira-bug-dashboard/</code>. Because there is no server there, the page runs in demo mode.</p>
<div class="callout tip"><span class="callout-title">Pushing a feature branch does not deploy</span>The workflow only runs for <code>main</code>, so pushing <code>feature/cloudflare-web-edition</code> changes nothing on the live demo. The Cloud edition is deployed separately with Wrangler.</div>

<h2>Merging the feature branch (when ready)</h2>
<pre><code>git checkout main
git merge --no-ff feature/cloudflare-web-edition
npm install &amp;&amp; npm run build &amp;&amp; (run the local tests)
git push origin main             # also redeploys the Pages demo</code></pre>
